  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a solemn funeral scene with uniformed officers carrying a casket draped in the Nigerian flag. The overlaid text reads, 'those who die in blue, are remembered forever.' The phrase 'die in blue' is a common tribute to law enforcement officers who sacrifice their lives in the line of duty, and the Nigerian flag signifies national pride and mourning. The overall intent is to honor fallen officers and evoke a sense of respect, remembrance, and patriotism. There is no toxicity present in this meme; it does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The intent is commemorative and respectful, using the visual of a state funeral and the symbolic flag to convey a message of enduring memory for those who serve and protect.",
